# rule.require.summary-at-the-cluster-root

> **when one subject splits into many subscopes, the summary is `$subject._.md` and each subscope is `$subject.$more.md`.**

`._.` marks a **cluster root**: the file that stands for the whole, as a peer of its own parts.

## .why — the root must sort first, and it must be addressable

| property | how `._.` gives it |
|---|---|
| **it sorts first** | `_` precedes every letter, so the root heads its cluster in any directory read |
| **it is computable** | know the subject, know the path — `$subject._.md`, no search |
| **it is globbable** | `*._.md` returns every cluster root; `$subject.*` returns the whole cluster |

## 🟡 .the summary is a PEER of its parts, never a parent

```
👍  term=route.stone._.choice._.md          # the root, a peer
    term=route.stone._.choice.reason.md
    term=route.stone._.choice.example=x.md

👎  term=stone/_.md                         # a directory, when none was needed
```

## .where it is already the convention

| when… | then… |
|---|---|
| a subject grows a **second** file | 🔴 that is the split. the first becomes `$subject._.md` |
| you write `$subject.readme.md` or `.overview.md` | rename it — the root has a name, and it sorts first |
| you write `$subject.md` beside `$subject.$zoom.md` | the bare name reads as one more zoom. mark the root |
| you reach for a **directory** for two files | do not — a flat cluster costs less and globs better |
| you write an **itemization** | the summary is its cluster root |

## .the test

> **"if a reader knew only the subject, could they compute the path to its summary?"** — no, they would read the directory and judge → the root is unmarked.

## .what the summary carries

the **whole**, plus an index of the parts. it does **not** narrate any one of them:

- what the subject is, shortest form that stands alone
- the axes along which it splits, when it splits along axes
- one line per part, with the fact that sets that part apart
- **the gaps** — the parts that are owed and absent

blocker: a subject split into parts with no `._.md` root (the whole has no address) · a root named `$subject.readme.md`, `.overview.md`, or bare `$subject.md` beside its own parts · a `._.md` root that narrates one part (eject it).
nitpick: a directory created for a cluster of two or three files.
false positive: a single file with no parts — the convention fires on the split, never before.

⇒ see also: `rule.prefer.decompose-a-subject-via-suffixes` (the WHETHER to this NAME) · `rule.forbid.itemization-without-coordinates` · `rule.require.catalog-is-an-index` · `rule.require.rules-are-clusters` · `template.domain-term` (learner).
